    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Ref # A Dictionary of Advanced Japanese Grammar p128 (Key sentence D)",
      "html": "<b>Ref #</b> A Dictionary of Advanced Japanese Grammar p128 (Key sentence D)",
      "credits_raw": "LR",
      "content_sha256": "0a5c6a65a8d183d2346e5425deec6070c991de9056b55b9ac01dd0a4b7971a32",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "理由（りゆう）の如何（いかん）によらず\nThis means \"no matter what reason there is.\"\nUsually, Japanese people say \"理由が何であろうとも\" instead.",
      "html": "理由（りゆう）の如何（いかん）によらず<br/>This means \"no matter what reason there is.\"<br/>Usually, Japanese people say \"理由が何であろうとも\" instead.",
      "credits_raw": "Nick",
      "content_sha256": "f3c830b477e17e8e60121dc80f32e32d214fa7377a48cdaf4b5f7dd1bfaab4bd",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "\"理由が何であろうとも\" would be used especially in speaking. In written form, \"いかんにもよらず\" is often seen.",
      "html": "\"理由が何であろうとも\" would be used especially in speaking. In written form, \"いかんにもよらず\" is often seen.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "ca61328e630d831ee8ddbe39533bef18f437eed3b3dddf44b9a6b9fb7184a227",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "A better translation for #5473 is \"The number of municipalities where you can take the employment test regardless of nationalty is increasing.",
      "html": "A better translation for #5473 is \"The number of municipalities where you can take the employment test regardless of nationalty is increasing.",
      "credits_raw": "samboki",
      "content_sha256": "32df76c02bdecd7d2b8fa1565d0cb957b9435e92c859353db922a9c6d11f54c2",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "@nikonniko Same meaning, different usage - as with a LOT of grammar. 名詞＋を問わず is a straight forward easy to use phrase, appropriate for most language situations. \n名詞＋の＋いかんを問わずis more formal, appropriate for written language, archaic?",
      "html": "@nikonniko Same meaning, different usage - as with a LOT of grammar. 名詞＋を問わず is a straight forward easy to use phrase, appropriate for most language situations. <br/>名詞＋の＋いかんを問わずis more formal, appropriate for written language, archaic?",
      "credits_raw": "LR",
      "content_sha256": "e9f49cedac85c0d70e436f99c37f93b56cab06176f731bfc8bb5ec0ec9d228b6",
